TEMPORARY FORK FOR VIVLIOSTYLE CLI

This fork exists solely to provide a patched MuPDF WASM package for Vivliostyle
CLI (https://github.com/vivliostyle/vivliostyle-cli/issues/732).

MuPDF used to truncate PDF Name objects longer than 127 bytes, which breaks
internal links in PDFs generated by Chromium. This has been fixed on the upstream
master branch (commit 966e928bad), but the fix has not been backported to the
1.27.x release branch. It will not be available until MuPDF 1.28.0 is released,
which based on the typical release cycle (6-7 months) is expected no earlier
than June 2026. This issue is already affecting real-world book projects that
rely on Vivliostyle CLI for PDF generation, and cannot wait for the next
official release.

This fork will be retired once the fix is included in an official MuPDF release.

References:
- https://github.com/vivliostyle/vivliostyle-cli/issues/732
- https://github.com/ArtifexSoftware/mupdf/commit/966e928bad3bd3f58ad92bbb9b34f05fa71d5805

---

BUILDING THE WASM PACKAGE

MuPDF's .gitmodules uses relative URLs for submodules. When cloning from this
fork, the URLs resolve to u1f992/* repositories that do not exist. To work
around this, temporarily point the remote to the upstream repository before
initializing submodules:

    $ git clone https://github.com/u1f992/mupdf.git -b patched-1.27.0
    $ cd mupdf
    $ git remote set-url origin https://github.com/ArtifexSoftware/mupdf.git
    $ git submodule sync --recursive
    $ git submodule update --init --recursive

Then build the WASM package using Docker (emsdk 4.0.8, as specified in
platform/wasm/tools/build.sh):

    $ docker pull emscripten/emsdk:4.0.8
    $ docker run --rm -v "$(pwd)":/src -w /src/platform/wasm emscripten/emsdk:4.0.8 \
      bash -c 'apt-get update -qq && apt-get install -y -qq brotli > /dev/null 2>&1 && npm install && EMSDK=/emsdk npm run prepack'

The built package is in platform/wasm/.

PUBLISHING TO NPM

The prerelease version requires an explicit dist-tag. Use --ignore-scripts to
skip the prepack script (build + compress), which has already been run inside
Docker:

    $ cd platform/wasm
    $ npm publish --ignore-scripts --tag patched --access public

This publishes @u1f992/mupdf@1.27.0-patched.1 under the "patched" dist-tag,
so it does not become the "latest" version. Users install it with:

    $ npm install @u1f992/mupdf@1.27.0-patched.1

To verify before publishing, add --dry-run:

    $ npm publish --dry-run --ignore-scripts --tag patched --access public

VERIFYING THE PATCH

The only difference from the official mupdf@1.27.0 WASM build should be the
name length limit change (127 -> 4095). This can be confirmed by comparing the
WebAssembly text representation:

First, download the official package:

    $ TEMPDIR=$(mktemp -d)
    $ npm pack mupdf@1.27.0 --pack-destination "$TEMPDIR"
    $ tar xzf "$TEMPDIR/mupdf-1.27.0.tgz" -C "$TEMPDIR"

Then compare the two binaries:

    $ docker run --rm \
      -v "$TEMPDIR/package/dist":/published:ro \
      -v "$(pwd)/platform/wasm/dist":/built:ro \
      emscripten/emsdk:4.0.8 bash -c '
        /emsdk/upstream/bin/wasm-dis /published/mupdf-wasm.wasm -o /tmp/published.wat &&
        /emsdk/upstream/bin/wasm-dis /built/mupdf-wasm.wasm -o /tmp/built.wat &&
        diff /tmp/published.wat /tmp/built.wat'

The diff output should only contain the following 5 changes, all within the
lex_name function. These correspond to the hardcoded 127-byte name length limit
being replaced with the 4095-byte PDF_MAX_NAME_LENGTH constant:

    414948c414948
    <      (i32.const 127)
    ---
    >      (i32.const 4095)
    414956c414956
    <       (i32.const 127)
    ---
    >       (i32.const 4095)
    414984c414984
    <        (i32.const 126)
    ---
    >        (i32.const 4094)
    415002c415002
    <           (i32.const 127)
    ---
    >           (i32.const 4095)
    415010c415010
    <            (i32.const 127)
    ---
    >            (i32.const 4095)

WHY THIS BASE COMMIT

The npm package mupdf@1.27.0 is labeled as version 1.27.0 in package.json, but
the embedded binary contains the version string "MuPDF 1.27.1":

    $ strings "$TEMPDIR/package/dist/mupdf-wasm.wasm" | grep "MuPDF 1\."
    MuPDF 1.27.1

This means the published binary was built not from the 1.27.0 Git tag but from
commit 7956afdc3 ("Bump patch release."), which only changes FZ_VERSION from
"1.27.0" to "1.27.1" in include/mupdf/fitz/version.h. Building from this
commit with emsdk 4.0.8 produces a WASM binary identical to the published one.
The patched-1.27.0 branch is therefore based on 7956afdc3 with the upstream fix
(966e928bad) cherry-picked on top

